{%- comment -%}
  fye-matching-band — the wedding band cut to sit against this ring.

  Built 01/09/2026, W917. Sits directly below fye-related-products.

  ── WHY THIS IS NOT fye-related-products WITH A SETTING ───────────────────

  It could have been: that section already reads this exact field and has a
  `source` toggle for it (Route A in the brief). It is a separate section for
  one measured reason — 1,184 of the 1,214 products with a band have EXACTLY
  ONE. A four-across product grid holding a single card is three empty columns
  of whitespace, which reads as a bug rather than as a recommendation.

  More importantly the claim is different. The related row says "you may also
  like"; this says "this is THE band for this ring" — Gemex cuts it to sit
  flush against that specific head. A grid tile cannot say that. So the card
  shows the two rings TOGETHER, which is the one thing a grid cannot do.

  ── THE DATA ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

      shopify--discovery--product_recommendation.complementary_products
      list.product_reference, capped at 10 by the Shopify definition
      1 entry for 1,184 products, 2–3 for 30

  **THE NAMESPACE MUST BE READ WITH BRACKETS.** It contains hyphens, which
  Liquid cannot parse in dot notation:

      product.metafields.shopify--discovery--product_recommendation   ✗ nil
      product.metafields['shopify--discovery--product_recommendation'] ✓

  The dotted form does not error — it silently returns nil, so the section
  looks permanently empty and the data looks like it never imported. Same trap
  documented in fye-related-products. Do not "tidy" either file to dots.

  ── MADE TO ORDER IS NOT UNAVAILABLE ──────────────────────────────────────

  Deliberate difference from fye-related-products, which skips products whose
  `available` is false. This section does NOT, because a made-to-order band is
  still THE band for this ring; hiding it would leave the pairing invisible
  for the sake of a stock flag that does not mean out of stock here. An
  unavailable band shows "Made to order" in place of the price and still links
  to its page, which is where the enquiry route lives.

  ── DIRECTION IS A SETTING, NOT A DETECTION ───────────────────────────────

  The import mirrors this relationship, so the band's own page shows the ring
  it belongs to — and "The matching band" is wrong wording there. The heading,
  note and link label are therefore per-template settings.

  It is NOT derived from product.type in Liquid. Per the brief: type is
  unreliable across this catalogue and has caused exactly this class of bug
  before. product.gemset.json (the eternity templates, where the bands live)
  carries the reversed wording.

  ── WHAT RENDERS NOTHING ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

  No entries, every entry nil or self-referential → no heading, no shell, no
  markup at all. 1,958 products have no band. product_reference keeps pointing
  at deleted products, so the nil guard is load-bearing.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign p = product

  assign ns = 'shopify--discovery--product_recommendation'
  assign bands = p.metafields[ns]['complementary_products'].value

  comment
    Collect handles rather than drops, so the render loop can re-resolve them
    and a nil entry cannot reach the card. Self-references are dropped: the
    mirror step in W918 should prevent them, but a product pointing at itself
    would render a ring paired with itself.
  endcomment
  assign picks = ''
  assign found = 0

  if bands != blank
    for item in bands
      if found >= s.count
        break
      endif
      unless item == blank or item.handle == p.handle
        assign picks = picks | append: item.handle | append: ','
        assign found = found | plus: 1
      endunless
    endfor
  endif

  assign handles = picks | split: ','

  comment
    The paired image — this ring beside the band — is what makes the block read
    as a pair. It only makes sense for a single band: repeating the same ring
    image down a list of three would say nothing and cost three renders.
  endcomment
  assign pair_media = false
  if s.show_pair and handles.size == 1 and p.featured_image != blank
    assign pair_media = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if handles.size > 0 -%}
  <section class="band band--{{ s.ground }} mband" data-screen-label="Matching band">
    <div class="wrap">
      {%- render 'sect-head',
            show: true,
            eyebrow: s.eyebrow,
            heading: s.heading,
            intro: s.note,
            align: s.align,
            flank: s.flank -%}

      <div class="mband__list">
        {%- for handle in handles -%}
          {%- assign item = all_products[handle] -%}
          {%- if item != blank -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign band_alt = item.featured_image.alt | default: item.title
              assign on_sale = false
              if item.compare_at_price > item.price
                assign on_sale = true
              endif
            -%}
            <a class="mband__card" href="{{ item.url }}">
              <span class="mband__media{% if pair_media %} mband__media--pair{% endif %}">
                {%- if pair_media -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    This ring first, the band second — left to right in the
                    order they are worn, and the order the shopper is thinking
                    in. aria-hidden: the ring is already the page's subject and
                    naming it again inside the band's link would mislead.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <span class="mband__shot mband__shot--this" aria-hidden="true">
                    {{ p.featured_image | image_url: width: 700 | image_tag:
                       loading: 'lazy',
                       widths: '240,360,480,700',
                       sizes: '(max-width: 749px) 45vw, 22vw',
                       alt: '',
                       class: 'mband__img' }}
                    <span class="mband__shotlbl">This ring</span>
                  </span>
                {%- endif -%}

                <span class="mband__shot">
                  {%- if item.featured_image != blank -%}
                    {{ item.featured_image | image_url: width: 700 | image_tag:
                       loading: 'lazy',
                       widths: '240,360,480,700',
                       sizes: '(max-width: 749px) 45vw, 22vw',
                       alt: band_alt,
                       class: 'mband__img' }}
                  {%- else -%}
                    <span class="mband__ph"></span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- if pair_media -%}
                    <span class="mband__shotlbl">The band</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </span>
              </span>

              <span class="mband__words">
                {%- if item.type != blank -%}
                  <span class="mband__type">{{ item.type }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}

                <span class="mband__name">{{ item.title }}</span>

                <span class="mband__price">
                  {%- if item.available == false -%}
                    Made to order
                  {%- elsif on_sale -%}
                    {{ item.price | money }}
                    <s class="mband__was">{{ item.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
                  {%- elsif item.price_varies -%}
                    From {{ item.price_min | money }}
                  {%- else -%}
                    {{ item.price | money }}
                  {%- endif -%}
                </span>

                {%- if s.cta_label != blank -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    Styled as a button but it is a span inside the card's own
                    anchor — a nested <a> would be invalid and would give
                    screen readers two links to the same place. The card is the
                    link; this is its affordance.

                    NOT an add-to-basket: the band needs its own metal, quality
                    and finger size chosen, so its product page is the only
                    honest destination.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <span class="btn btn--outline mband__cta">{{ s.cta_label }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
/* One wide card per band, stacked. No carousel for three items, and no
   two-across: a full-width card is what makes this read as a pairing rather
   than as another grid. */
.fye .mband__list {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s5);
}

.fye .mband .sect-head {
  margin-bottom: var(--s7);
}

/* Media beside words. The media column is the larger share because the
   pairing is the argument — the shopper decides from the two images. */
.fye .mband__card {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: var(--s7);
  align-items: center;
  padding: var(--s5);
  background: var(--white);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  transition: border-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}

.fye .mband__card:hover {
  border-color: var(--sage);
}

.fye .mband__media {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: var(--s4);
}

/* Two shots side by side, in the order the rings are worn. */
.fye .mband__media--pair {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
}

.fye .mband__shot {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s2);
}

.fye .mband__img,
.fye .mband__ph {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  object-fit: cover;
  background: var(--ivory);
  transition: transform var(--dur) var(--ease);
}

.fye .mband__card:hover .mband__img {
  transform: scale(1.02);
}

/* Clipped so the hover scale cannot bleed past the square edge. */
.fye .mband__shot {
  overflow: hidden;
}

.fye .mband__shotlbl {
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

/* The current ring is context, not the offer, so its shot is quieter. */
.fye .mband__shot--this .mband__img {
  opacity: 0.82;
}

.fye .mband__words {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: var(--s2);
}

.fye .mband__type {
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .mband__name {
  font-size: var(--fs-h5);
  color: var(--ink);
  text-wrap: pretty;
  transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}

.fye .mband__card:hover .mband__name {
  color: var(--sage);
}

.fye .mband__price {
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  color: var(--ink);
}

.fye .mband__was {
  margin-inline-start: var(--s2);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .mband__cta {
  margin-top: var(--s3);
}

@media (max-width: 749px) {
  /* Media above words. The pair stays side by side within it — shrinking two
     squares is better than losing the comparison that is the whole point. */
  .fye .mband__card {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--s5);
    padding: var(--s4);
  }

  .fye .mband__cta {
    width: 100%;
    text-align: center;
  }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Matching band",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "fye-matching-band",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Reads the product's Search & Discovery complementary products — the band Gemex cuts to sit against this ring. Renders nothing when the product has none. The relationship is mirrored, so a band's own page shows its ring: set the wording per template rather than expecting one heading to work both ways."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "count",
      "label": "Maximum to show",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 3,
      "info": "1,184 products have exactly one; 30 have two or three."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_pair",
      "label": "Show this ring beside the band",
      "info": "Only when there is a single band — repeating the ring image down a list says nothing.",
      "default": true
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Wording" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Wear them together" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "The matching band" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "note",
      "label": "Note",
      "default": "Shaped to sit flush against this ring.",
      "info": "One line. This is the sentence that makes it a service rather than a cross-sell."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Link label", "default": "View the matching band" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "align",
      "label": "Alignment",
      "options": [
        { "value": "center", "label": "Centred" },
        { "value": "left", "label": "Left" }
      ],
      "default": "center"
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "flank", "label": "Hairlines either side of the heading", "default": true },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Band" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "ground",
      "label": "Background",
      "options": [
        { "value": "white", "label": "White" },
        { "value": "ivory", "label": "Champagne ivory" }
      ],
      "default": "white",
      "info": "The related products row above is ivory, so white keeps the two blocks apart."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Matching band" }]
}
{% endschema %}
